# Phase 3: The Native Driver Switch - CashBank Slice

This plan focuses on Phase 3 of the Mongoose migration for the `finance` module: completely replacing Mongoose queries with the native `mongodb` driver in the Repository layer, and linking native TypeScript interfaces directly to our Zod schemas.

## Proposed Changes

### Dependencies
#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/package.json)
- Add the official MongoDB native driver via `npm install mongodb`.

### Database Connection Management
#### [NEW] [db.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/config/db.ts) (or modify existing connection)
- Ensure we export a shared `mongodb` [Db](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/repositories/CashBankRepository.ts#9-13) instance or `MongoClient` instance to be injected or retrieved by the Repositories, replacing `mongoose.connection`. If an existing `db.ts` file manages the connection, it will be augmented to export the native DB instance alongside Mongoose (temporarily, until Mongoose is fully uninstalled from other modules).

### Finance Domain
- Refactor the data access layer and model interfaces to sever ties with Mongoose `Document`.

#### [MODIFY] [CashBankSchemas.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/modules/finance/schemas/CashBankSchemas.ts)
- Export Zod inferred types to be used across the application:
  ```typescript
  export type CreateAccountDTO = z.infer<typeof CreateAccountSchema>['body'];
  ```

#### [MODIFY] [IBankAccount.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/interfaces/IBankAccount.ts), [ICheque.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/interfaces/ICheque.ts), [ICashbankTransaction.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/interfaces/ICashbankTransaction.ts)
- Remove `extends Document` from Mongoose.
- Convert `_id` and other relational fields from `mongoose.Types.ObjectId` to native `ObjectId` imported from `mongodb`.

#### [MODIFY] [CashBankRepository.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/repositories/CashBankRepository.ts)
- Switch all queries from Mongoose Model methods (`BankAccount.find()`, `Cheque.create()`) to Native Collection methods (`db.collection('bank_accounts').find()`, `db.collection('cheques').insertOne()`).
- Explicitly cast string IDs to native `new ObjectId(id)` where necessary for MongoDB queries.
- Update `$lookup` aggregations if any `.populate()` calls existed (none currently observed in Phase 1 for this slice, but we will ensure joins are handled natively if needed).
- Map MongoDB's `_id` securely to string representations when returning to the Service layer to prevent serialization issues.

#### [MODIFY] [CashBankService.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/modules/finance/services/CashBankService.ts)
- Remove any lingering `.toObject()` calls, as the native driver returns plain JavaScript objects directly.
- Ensure all returned data matches the expected boundaries without Mongoose wrapping.

