## Phase 4: ACID Transactions (Native MongoDB)

Once the native driver is in place, multi-step operations like Transfers and Cash Transactions need to be wrapped in native MongoDB transactions to ensure atomic consistency.

### Proposed Architecture for Transactions
#### [MODIFY] [CashBankRepository.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/repositories/CashBankRepository.ts)
- Add a helper method `executeInTransaction<T>(callback: (session: ClientSession) => Promise<T>): Promise<T>` to manage the lifecycle of a native `ClientSession`.
- Update all existing data mutation methods ([createTransaction](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/repositories/CashBankRepository.ts#108-118), [updateBalance](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/repositories/CashBankRepository.ts#96-102), [createCheque](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/repositories/CashBankRepository.ts#184-193), etc.) to accept an optional `session?: ClientSession` argument.
- Pass this `session` directly to the underlying `collection.insertOne(..., { session })` or `collection.updateOne(..., { session })` methods.

#### [MODIFY] [CashBankService.ts](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/modules/finance/services/CashBankService.ts)
- Identify all methods that write to multiple documents or collections:
  - [createTransfer](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/modules/finance/services/CashBankService.ts#82-109) (creates transaction, updates two account balances)
  - [createCashTransaction](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/modules/finance/services/CashBankService.ts#110-149) (creates transaction, updates one account balance)
  - [updateChequeStatus](file:///c:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/modules/finance/services/CashBankService.ts#349-374) (creates transaction, updates account balance, updates cheque)
- Wrap these operations inside `this.cashBankRepository.executeInTransaction(async (session) => { ... })`.
- Pass the `session` object to all subsequent repository calls made within the callback.

